      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also have this issue, I'm unable to figure out a fix for it.\n\nThings I've tried.\n\n* Reinstalling my ethernet driver.\n\n* Swapping routers.\n\n* Reinstalling SteamVR.\n\n* Reinstalling SteamLink.\n\n* Updating my GPU Drivers multiple times.\n\n* Using a bandwidth cap in SteamLink.\n\n* Setting my DNS to cloudflares.\n\n* Disabling Windows 11 Hardware Acceleration.\n\n* Allowing VRC through the firewall.\n\n* Disabling IPv6.\n\n* Reinstalling VRChat.\n\n* Clearing the VRC Cache.\n\n* Changed my systems power plan to high performance.\n\n* Set my etherenet device to never power off.\n\n* Turned off energy saver/green mode on the etherenet adapter.\n\nNothing has worked. For now I'm stuck using AirLink which sucks and get extremely laggy over a play session and then Virtual Desktop, which is ok but really no matter how you configure the settings doesn't look as good as SteamLink. I want to use SteamLink again, but VRC or Valve really needs to fix this issue. \n\nAlso I never had this issue until I upgraded my CPU and Mobo from a 11950h to an AMD Ryzen 9900X, and installed Windows 11 (Before I was using Windows 10). Before I did this I didn't have the issue with SteamLink. Which somewhat makes me think it's a Windows 11 compatibility problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
