      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c9bfccf37d9d113629fc658|full_name} In my post below I highlighted that this issue with SteamLink is that it is too demanding on the network you're using, causing other things on the network to be drowned out. To keep using SteamLink, it has to be limited in some way to not cause everything else to get interrupted. Unfortunately, besides finding this is the cause, I just accepted that Virtual Desktop was the option that worked out the box with significantly less effort for me.",
